Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: Kumbaga, interrelated po ang mga sektor na ito sa paggalaw ng kuryente sa ating bansa.

2603
03:03:35,320 --> 03:03:40,840
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: Habang pataas ng pataas ang kuryente, pataas din ng pataas ang presyo ng bilihin.

2604
03:03:41,680 --> 03:03:47,780
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: Dahil kailangan may pasa ito ng mga sektor sa nabanggit kong mga consumers.

2605
03:03:47,780 --> 03:03:50,780
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: At ang pagdaloy o...

2606
03:03:51,220 --> 03:03:54,500
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: pass-through ay nagdudulot ng pagtaas na inflation.

2607
03:03:55,180 --> 03:03:59,740
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: How does the Banko Sentral ng Pilipinas resolve these issues of rising inflation?

2608
03:04:00,000 --> 03:04:00,700
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: Thank you, Madam Chair.

2609
03:04:04,080 --> 03:04:06,160
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Deputy Governor, may please respond.

2610
03:04:07,080 --> 03:04:09,040
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Thank you, Madam Chair.

2611
03:04:11,440 --> 03:04:19,780
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Talaga naman hong sinusubaybayan rin namin yung mga paggalaw ng iba't ibang components noong ating Consumer Price Index.

2612
03:04:20,540 --> 03:04:21,200
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Kung saan.

2613
03:04:21,200 --> 03:04:26,060
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Kung saan yun yung nagiging batayan sa pag-compute noong ating inflation rate.

2614
03:04:26,780 --> 03:04:29,620
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Isa na ho dito yung sa electricity rates.

2615
03:04:30,080 --> 03:04:31,580
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: So tinitignan ho namin yun.

2616
03:04:32,300 --> 03:04:42,440
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: At tinitignan rin ho kung ito ba ay nagdudulot ng tinatawag na spillover sa iba pang mga presyo.

2617
03:04:42,720 --> 03:04:48,480
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Paggalaw ng mga iba pang presyo na binibili ng ating mga kababayan.

2618
03:04:49,320 --> 03:04:50,480
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Ito ho ay...

2619
03:04:51,200 --> 03:04:56,880
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Closely, time team na tinitignan ho namin.

2620
03:04:57,480 --> 03:05:02,740
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Gaya ho nang sinabi namin kanina, ang inflation rate ho at ganoon rin ho yung debt-debt.

2621
03:05:03,340 --> 03:05:07,960
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Nakita ho na ito ay, ang average ho ay 5% this year.

2622
03:05:08,680 --> 03:05:15,280
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Ngunit nung huling mga dalawang buwan, ito ay 6.4%, 6.2%.

2623
03:05:15,280 --> 03:05:20,720
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Ang iba nito ho ay dulot rin rin noong sinasabi ninyong pag-akyat.

2624
03:05:21,200 --> 03:05:26,960
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Noong ating inflation, o positive na inflation sa electricity rates.

2625
03:05:27,440 --> 03:05:29,800
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: So ito ho ay tinitignan namin ng mabuti.

2626
03:05:30,260 --> 03:05:33,420
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: At sa aming outlook po na binigay kanina,

2627
03:05:33,420 --> 03:05:45,080
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: ang pagsusuri ho namin, maaaring mag-average ng 6.4% this year ang ating inflation rate.

2628
03:05:45,960 --> 03:05:49,500
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Kasama na ho dyan yung epekto noong pagtaas,

2629
03:05:49,620 --> 03:05:50,420
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: o yung mataas na...

2630
03:05:51,200 --> 03:05:55,820
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: presyo ng krudo sa international na merkado.

2631
03:05:56,500 --> 03:06:04,160
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: At ito ho, kasama na rin dyan yung epekto ho nito sa ating gasolina at saka sa electricity.

2632
03:06:04,480 --> 03:06:10,540
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Kaya ho, medyo mataas yung nakikitang average na inflation ho itong taon na to.

2633
03:06:12,380 --> 03:06:13,160
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Salamat po.

2634
03:06:13,160 --> 03:06:17,220
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Thank you, Madam Chair. Thank you sa Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas for that response.

2635
03:06:17,720 --> 03:06:19,140
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Maraming salamat po, Madam Chair. That's all.

2636
03:06:21,200 --> 03:06:22,340
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Thank you very much, Representative Pleyto.

2637
03:06:22,580 --> 03:06:27,740
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: We'll now move to our next interpolator from the minority, the Honorable Antonio Tinio.

2638
03:06:30,740 --> 03:06:32,740
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Thank you, Madam Chair.

2639
03:06:33,360 --> 03:06:40,220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Madam Chair, unang set ng questions tungkol sa sweldo, salary increase.

2640
03:06:40,620 --> 03:06:42,280
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Matindi ang crisis ngayon.

2641
03:06:43,540 --> 03:06:51,180
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At para sa mga, lalo na mga empleyado sa civilian, para sa kanila sa kapos ang salary increase,

2642
03:06:51,200 --> 03:06:54,500
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: kahit in-implement ang 3rd tranche and then next year, 4th tranche.

2643
03:06:55,160 --> 03:07:03,880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kung DBM ang tatanungin, 4th tranche na next year, kailan ang susunod na round ng salary increase na maasahan?

2644
03:07:06,780 --> 03:07:14,620
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Madam Chair, Your Honor, bahagi po ng mandato ng DBM yung patuloy na pag-evaluate po ng ating salary schedule.

2645
03:07:14,620 --> 03:07:20,040
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: At dito po sa... meron po tayo ngayong ikukomisyon ng ongoing na pag-aaral,

2646
03:07:20,120 --> 03:07:21,120
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: kahit po meron pa tayo...

2647
03:07:21,200 --> 03:07:25,820
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: yung 4th tranche na inaasahang i-implement by 2027,

2648
03:07:26,360 --> 03:07:30,260
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: particular na nga po precisely because of the point of the Honorable Tinio,

2649
03:07:30,360 --> 03:07:33,820
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: upang malaman po natin yung magiging susunod na schedule.

2650
03:07:34,100 --> 03:07:38,220
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So, dito po natin sa pag-aaral po malalaman, Madam Chair, Your Honor,

2651
03:07:38,700 --> 03:07:42,940
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: kung ano po yung magiging timing, amount of increase, if any,

2652
03:07:43,460 --> 03:07:47,400
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: pagkatapos po ng ating gagawin na compensation study.

2653
03:07:48,220 --> 03:07:49,260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kailan po ang study na yan?

2654
03:07:51,200 --> 03:07:59,880
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Meron po tayo, Your Honor, Madam Chair, na isa sa gawa na study together with the GCG early next year.

2655
03:08:00,380 --> 03:08:02,000
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This year, Your Honor.

2656
03:08:03,000 --> 03:08:04,560
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At kailan po maasahan ng result?

2657
03:08:05,280 --> 03:08:13,960
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We are expecting, Your Honor, a result by the second half of next year, Madam Chair, Your Honor.

2658
03:08:13,960 --> 03:08:15,320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Second half of next year.

2659
03:08:15,560 --> 03:08:21,040
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, mula doon, babatay kung may pag... magkakaroon ng...

2660
03:08:21,040 --> 03:08:24,380
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ng susunod o kailan magkakaroon, ganun ba? At kung magkano?

2661
03:08:25,240 --> 03:08:26,460
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Yes, Madam Chair, Your Honor.

2662
03:08:26,680 --> 03:08:32,300
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: At sisikapin po natin na if there will be a result of the assessment,

2663
03:08:32,740 --> 03:08:39,100
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: sisikapin po natin na ito ay makonsidera din sa magiging submission po ng budget for 2028.

2664
03:08:39,300 --> 03:08:43,600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Kung magkano man po or kung kailan po yung lalabas doon sa ating pag-aaral.

2665
03:08:43,600 --> 03:08:46,480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, if ever 2028 pa. Okay.

2666
03:08:47,220 --> 03:08:48,600
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Punta tayo sa pera.

2667
03:08:49,640 --> 03:08:50,600
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, marami na po nagsasabi.

2668
03:08:51,040 --> 03:08:56,740
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 2009 pa po, huling natakda yung 2,000 peso sa month na pera.

2669
03:08:57,720 --> 03:09:02,980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At ito ang isang posibleng pagtugon doon sa kakapusan.

2670
03:09:03,140 --> 03:09:05,660
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Dahil nga tumaas ang inflation, sinasabi nyo rin naman.

2671
03:09:08,520 --> 03:09:14,840
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: May posibilidad po ba na magtaas ng pera sa 2027 budget?

2672
03:09:15,240 --> 03:09:20,840
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Madam Chair, Your Honor, unlike po yung sa comprehensive salary increase na talagang...

2673
03:09:21,040 --> 03:09:27,000
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: nangailangan ng mas malalim na pag-aaral, ito pong posibilidad ng pag-increase ng pera.

2674
03:09:27,140 --> 03:09:30,540
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Ginagawa po ngayon ang pag-aaral ngayon na po mismo ng DBM

2675
03:09:30,540 --> 03:09:37,020
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: upang kami po ay makapagbigay ng necessary recommendation sa ating presidente

2676
03:09:37,020 --> 03:09:43,200
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: kung magkakaroon man po ng adjustment sa pera ay kung hanggang saan po yung ire-recommend ang increase.

2677
03:09:43,200 --> 03:09:50,980
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Ito pong pag-aaral tungkol sa pera, ang tinatarget po natin ay makapagkaroon po tayo ng recommendation sa ating presidente.

2678
03:09:51,040 --> 03:09:53,040
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Bago po matapos itong taon na ito.

2679
03:09:53,840 --> 03:09:55,940
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: For implementation in 2027?

2680
03:09:57,340 --> 03:10:00,840
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Yun po ang isang target, Madam Chair, Your Honor.

2681
03:10:01,220 --> 03:10:09,480
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Kung magkakaroon man po ng adjustment sa pera, ito po ay ating sisikapi na ma-accommodate sa 2027

2682
03:10:09,480 --> 03:10:15,440
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: sa ilalim po ng ating Miscellaneous Personal Benefits Fund, Madam Chair, Your Honor.

2683
03:10:15,780 --> 03:10:21,020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay, so tututukan po natin yan. So 2027, pagtaas ng pera.

2684
03:10:21,040 --> 03:10:27,580
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Iba na ako, mahigpit ang oras natin. Meron po tayong ilang slides.

2685
03:10:30,340 --> 03:10:31,280
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sigil muna yung time.

2686
03:10:34,040 --> 03:10:35,680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Tumatakbo yung oras, Chair.

2687
03:10:39,840 --> 03:10:41,180
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay, ito na po.

2688
03:10:41,180 --> 03:10:50,300
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay, so kaugnay sa flood control, of course, yan ang nasa isip ng mamamayan.

2689
03:10:51,040 --> 03:10:59,240
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Especially in 2023, 2024, and 2025, talagang lumobo ng gusto ang pondo sa flood control

2690
03:10:59,240 --> 03:11:05,880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: at malaki ang dahilan niyan, isang malaking dahilan niyan, yung congressional insertions.

2691
03:11:06,560 --> 03:11:11,040
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ngayon, sa congressional insertions, para mangyari yan, para madagdagan ng DPWH,

2692
03:11:11,860 --> 03:11:18,220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: kailangan may bawasan sa ibang ahensya o pondo. Tama po ba? Di ba ganun?

2693
03:11:19,040 --> 03:11:20,380
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Madam Chair, Your Honor.

2694
03:11:21,040 --> 03:11:25,260
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Susunod po sa zero-sum principle at dahil pareho po ang total ng budget. Tama po.

2695
03:11:25,820 --> 03:11:27,520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay, now, next slide.

2696
03:11:29,020 --> 03:11:35,740
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Meron tayong napansin na pattern at sabihin ko pa nga, modus, ng padding under the neb.

2697
03:11:36,560 --> 03:11:38,240
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Padding of certain items.

2698
03:11:39,040 --> 03:11:48,740
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ito yung over the years, palaging malaki sa NEP, tapos pagdating sa GAA, lumiliit na significantly.

2699
03:11:49,460 --> 03:11:50,740
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At sa tingin natin, ito yung...

2700
03:11:51,040 --> 03:11:57,460
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ito yung pinanggagalingan, o ito yung, this is what enables massive insertions.

2701
03:11:57,900 --> 03:11:58,580
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, ano po ito?

2702
03:11:59,200 --> 03:12:05,480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Isa dyan, yung mga foreign assisted projects sa DOTR at saka sa DPWH.

2703
03:12:07,480 --> 03:12:14,080
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: I will not detail it too much, pero nakikita nyo, yung padding or buffer na sinasabi dyan,

2704
03:12:14,080 --> 03:12:21,000
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: umaabot sa for 2026, for example.

2705
03:12:21,040 --> 03:12:27,520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Nag-propose kayo sa NEP under DOTR ng foreign assisted, 135 billion.

2706
03:12:28,060 --> 03:12:30,520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sa GAA, naging 64 billion na lang ito.

2707
03:12:30,920 --> 03:12:36,440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And you can work back by mas malalaki pang examples ng padding dito.

2708
03:12:36,760 --> 03:12:37,360
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Next slide.

2709
03:12:39,020 --> 03:12:48,300
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Isa pang ginagamit for padding, for insertions, ay miscellaneous personnel benefits fund and pension and gratuity fund.

2710
03:12:48,300 --> 03:12:51,000
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ang pattern over the years, napakalaki.

2711
03:12:51,000 --> 03:12:57,160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Nang sinasabmit nyo sa NEP, tapos pagdating sa GAA, napaka significantly less.

2712
03:12:58,880 --> 03:13:08,000
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And ngayon, ang tanong po ay notable ngayon sa DOTR, napakalaki po nang sinabit nyong additional budget.

2713
03:13:08,800 --> 03:13:14,240
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: From 84 billion to something like almost 300 billion.

2714
03:13:15,220 --> 03:13:17,880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At malaki doon ay foreign assisted.

2715
03:13:17,880 --> 03:13:20,880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, ang tanong ko, mauulit na naman.

2716
03:13:21,000 --> 03:13:21,540
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ano naman ba ito?

2717
03:13:22,760 --> 03:13:33,300
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ang laki sa simula, nung proposal nyo, tapos sa dulo, maliit na yan, at ginamit na yung fiscal space for insertions.

2718
03:13:35,240 --> 03:13:42,840
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Madam Chair, Your Honor, on the part of the DBM, we most respectfully submit na yun pong amounts that we propose in the NEP

2719
03:13:42,840 --> 03:13:50,840
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: ay naaayon po doon sa aming evaluated requirement para po sa mga foreign assisted projects na ito.

2720
03:13:51,000 --> 03:14:00,460
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So, in fact, ngayon po hawak ko yung detalye, mas mababa pa po yung aming proposed level sa NEP kung ikukumpara po sa actual agency proposal.

2721
03:14:00,700 --> 03:14:07,920
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: As to the point, Madam Chair, Your Honor, na kung bakit po ito ay eventually nababawasan, we most respectfully submit.

2722
03:14:07,920 --> 03:14:17,640
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: In fact, Your Honor, ito po yung reason, one of the reasons kung bakit din po nadidelay yung implementation ng ating mga foreign assisted projects.

2723
03:14:17,780 --> 03:14:20,980
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Dahil po on the part of the executive, yun pong aming submitted.

2724
03:14:21,000 --> 03:14:30,860
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: At yung foreign assisted level po talaga yung sa tingin naming kinakailangan para masiguro pong on track and on time yung implementation ng ating iba't ibang mga foreign assisted projects.

2725
03:14:32,540 --> 03:14:39,240
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Well, anyway, ang punto, nakatutok po tayo sa mga pondong yan at tignan natin kung ano mangyayari sa dulo.

2726
03:14:39,540 --> 03:14:45,500
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ang tanong ko po, magkakaroon na naman po ba ng massive insertion sa budget na ito?

2727
03:14:51,000 --> 03:15:01,140
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Madam Chair, Your Honor, in as much as we have already submitted the NEP, sa amin po ay nasa kongreso na po ang kapalaran po ng National Expenditure Program.

2728
03:15:01,460 --> 03:15:03,160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, hindi kayo magsasubmit ng IRATA?

2729
03:15:04,500 --> 03:15:08,800
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: As far as the DBM is concerned, Your Honor, wala po kami ngayong pinag-uusap.

2730
03:15:09,940 --> 03:15:11,100
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay, next slide.

2731
03:15:12,900 --> 03:15:13,580
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Next slide.

2732
03:15:15,440 --> 03:15:16,900
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kaugnay sa flood control.

2733
03:15:17,340 --> 03:15:20,980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ang isang kapansin-pansin po ay binalik po ang flood control ngayon.

2734
03:15:21,000 --> 03:15:33,020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ang isang napansin po natin dito sa listahan ng DBM ay, next slide,

2735
03:15:35,020 --> 03:15:44,400
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: out of 197 district engineering offices, kung flood control lang, 113 lang po na DEO ang merong flood control projects.

2736
03:15:45,520 --> 03:15:48,780
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At ngayon, bakit ganun?

2737
03:15:49,500 --> 03:15:50,980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sabi na, baka wala, hindi kayo isubmit.

2738
03:15:51,000 --> 03:15:53,680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kailangan ng ibang distrito yung flood control projects.

2739
03:15:53,860 --> 03:16:06,160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: But, isang kapansin-pansin po, the whole of Region 11, meaning the Davao region, wala po ni isang flood control projects, blanco po.

2740
03:16:06,680 --> 03:16:12,000
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: If you can go back to the previous, ayan, o, kita niyo may blanco dun sa Region 11.

2741
03:16:15,360 --> 03:16:16,220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Nagtataka kami.

2742
03:16:17,280 --> 03:16:20,740
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kasi binabaha naman sa Davao, alam natin, pero wala.

2743
03:16:21,000 --> 03:16:23,480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. Bakit po ganun?

2744
03:16:24,760 --> 03:16:33,020
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Madam Chair, Your Honor, ang naging assessment at evaluation po ng DBM ay nakabatay po doon sa proposal na ipinadala ng DPWH.

2745
03:16:33,520 --> 03:16:41,160
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So, on our part po, Madam Chair, Your Honor, kung wala pong proposal na ipinadala from DPWH, ay wala rin po kaming i-evaluate.

2746
03:16:41,160 --> 03:16:47,340
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So, probably on this question, Madam Chair, Your Honor, we can also defer later on to DPWH

2747
03:16:47,340 --> 03:16:50,900
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: para mabigyan po ng mas malinaw na paliwanag kung,

2748
03:16:51,000 --> 03:16:54,060
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: bakit hindi po, kung meron pong gaps na ganito po na na-observe.

2749
03:16:54,080 --> 03:16:59,500
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. Well, nagtataka po tayo, no, dahil hindi lang naman Davao region, pero ito buong region.

2750
03:17:00,060 --> 03:17:07,240
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No, sabi ko nga, there are 47 regions in total, DEOs, in total na zero.

2751
03:17:08,040 --> 03:17:16,000
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, ang point ko, eh, malamang magsasubmit pa yan, di ba, at magkakaroon ng irata.

2752
03:17:16,620 --> 03:17:20,560
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, sabi nyo kanina, walang irata as far as you're concerned.

2753
03:17:20,560 --> 03:17:21,380
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: We shall see.

2754
03:17:21,940 --> 03:17:26,980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. In other words, ang pangamba natin dito ay magkakaroon na naman ng insertions

2755
03:17:26,980 --> 03:17:33,620
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: at yung sinasabing yung reforms na may vetting and so on and so forth, ay hindi mangyayari pagkaganon.

2756
03:17:34,140 --> 03:17:40,580
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Now, another question, yung sinabi ni Secretary Bonoan na may leadership fund.

2757
03:17:41,440 --> 03:17:45,060
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Meron po ba ang leadership fund dito sa budget na ito?

2758
03:17:46,680 --> 03:17:48,380
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Wala po, Madam Chair, Your Honor.

2759
03:17:48,680 --> 03:17:49,380
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Wala po.

2760
03:17:49,380 --> 03:17:52,520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Wala po. Okay. Balik po sa kaninang slide.

2761
03:17:53,640 --> 03:18:06,260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Bakit po sa DPWH budget, flood control lang ito, merong nakalodge sa central office na as much as 40, is that 49 billion pesos?

2762
03:18:07,260 --> 03:18:18,460
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Tapos, sabi nyo kanina, yung mga nasa central office, yung hindi pa ma-allocate to the regions at the time of budget preparation.

2763
03:18:19,380 --> 03:18:26,640
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: However, that's not true because as you can see, yung nasa central office, ay nakadistribute din sa regions.

2764
03:18:28,520 --> 03:18:35,140
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Bakit ganyan ang budget nyo? Merong nasa regions, tapos merong nasa central office, pero may region din.

2765
03:18:35,980 --> 03:18:40,220
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: To the Honorable Tinio, may we request that to be the last question.

2766
03:18:40,220 --> 03:18:41,060
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. Sige po.

2767
03:18:41,400 --> 03:18:46,220
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So, we'll request Secretary Kim de Leon to respond and then we'll move to the next interpellator.

2768
03:18:47,260 --> 03:18:49,220
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Madam Chair, Your Honor, isa pong malaking bahagi.

2769
03:18:49,380 --> 03:18:55,400
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Ang mga proyektong na kailalim po sa central office ay itong ating mga foreign-assisted projects.

2770
03:18:55,500 --> 03:19:06,580
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: By default po, Madam Chair, Your Honor, hindi lang po sa DPWH, gayon din po sa iba pang mga ahensya, kapag po foreign-assisted project, ito po ay nakatag under sa respective central offices.

2771
03:19:06,800 --> 03:19:17,200
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So, yung balansi po nito, ito po ay mga proyekto na isinumiti po ng DPWH and they properly tag it po sa central office based on their respective assessments.

2772
03:19:17,260 --> 03:19:19,200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: I can assure you, these are not...

2773
03:19:19,380 --> 03:19:22,860
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: These are not foreign-assisted projects. Walang pinag-iba yan.

2774
03:19:23,500 --> 03:19:29,980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Mga tig-150, tig-80 million na flood control projects, walang pinag-iba sa mga project ng distrito.

2775
03:19:30,680 --> 03:19:35,900
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, I will... Ako, ang sasabihin ko, yan yung leadership fund na nasa central office.

2776
03:19:36,280 --> 03:19:44,280
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. Yamang ganun, ang punto ko po rito ay binalik ang flood control, pero dating gawi pa rin.

2777
03:19:44,280 --> 03:19:48,600
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No? Nandyan pa rin yung mga iniintay, nakaabang.

2778
03:19:49,380 --> 03:19:56,100
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Para sa insertions at merong allocation na tinawag ni Bonoan na leadership fund.

2779
03:19:56,100 --> 03:20:13,940
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, ang huling punto ko na lang po, Madam Chair, ay malinaw para sa kinatawang ito na walang anumang substantial na pagbabago sa proseso ng pagpondo, pag-identify pagpondo ng flood control projects.

2780
03:20:14,480 --> 03:20:19,000
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Therefore, dapat hindi pa ito ibalik sa kasalukuyang budget.

2781
03:20:19,380 --> 03:20:25,000
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Tip na flood control, dapat ilagay sa classrooms.

2782
03:20:25,520 --> 03:20:25,640
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No?

2783
03:20:25,640 --> 03:20:27,580
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: My very last slide, Madam Chair.

2784
03:20:28,680 --> 03:20:39,180
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ang target na sa inyong budget, ang target na ipatay yun yung classroom for this year is, for next year, 2027, is 700.

2785
03:20:41,940 --> 03:20:46,380
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, nagbalik kayo ng mahigit 100 billion in flood control.

2786
03:20:46,380 --> 03:20:48,260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Samantala, ang target...

2787
03:20:48,260 --> 03:20:48,540
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ayan, no?

2788
03:20:49,380 --> 03:20:50,120
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Nakalagay mismo.

2789
03:20:50,120 --> 03:20:57,120
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: The target na classrooms na gusto niyong ipatayo para sa taong ito ay 700 lamang.

2790
03:21:00,860 --> 03:21:02,400
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Thank you, Representative Tinio.

2791
03:21:02,960 --> 03:21:11,880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, ang punto po, sa halip na flood control, ilagay ang pondo sa classroom dahil 160,000 ang shortage ng classrooms, Madam Chair.

2792
03:21:12,020 --> 03:21:13,180
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Thank you, Representative Tinio.

2793
03:21:13,180 --> 03:21:14,260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 160,000.

2794
03:21:14,500 --> 03:21:16,880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: That would be the last question for this round.

2795
03:21:16,880 --> 03:21:17,880
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: A response from...

2796
03:21:19,380 --> 03:21:20,260
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Can you explain?

2797
03:21:20,560 --> 03:21:21,600
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: A response lang po, Madam Chair.

2798
03:21:21,600 --> 03:21:29,120
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: If Secretary De Leon would like to respond shortly, like a brief response to the query of Hon. Pleyto.

2799
03:21:29,240 --> 03:21:33,780
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Madam Chair, Your Honor, dalawang mahalagang factor po patungkol po sa budget sa classroom.

2800
03:21:33,940 --> 03:21:39,760
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Una po, yun pong 2026 budget of DepEd for classroom, yung kanilang absorptive capacity.

2801
03:21:40,220 --> 03:21:48,440
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Ngayong second half pa lang po sila nag-uumpisang ma-implement yung kanilang nakalaang budget po para sa kanila na inaasahan pong magsispeel over.

2802
03:21:48,500 --> 03:21:49,220
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Hanggang 2026.

2803
03:21:49,380 --> 03:22:05,220
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Ang pangalawa pong mahalagang factor, Madam Chair, Your Honor, is by 2027, meron din po tayong isang package ng classroom infrastructure, school infrastructure project na tinatarget po nating ma-implement through a public-private partnership.

2804
03:22:05,220 --> 03:22:19,220
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So ito po ay meron po tayong target na ah ito po yung PIP 3 na may estimated project cost na 105.7 billion na labas po on top po of our general appropriations act being a public

2805
03:22:19,380 --> 03:22:22,680
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: private partnership. Your Honor.

2806
03:22:22,680 --> 03:22:33,680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Thank you, Madam Chair. Pag ah flood pag classroom hirap ma-implement pag flood control parang hindi. Yun lang po ang last comment ko, Madam Chair. Thank you.

2807
03:22:33,680 --> 03:22:49,360
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Again, sorry we've given you like 6 minutes 6 minutes 42 seconds over the time. So we move to the next interpellator from the majority representative Ryan Ro. Thank you, Madam Chair.

2808
03:22:49,380 --> 03:22:58,070
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: Hello. Hello. Uh, good afternoon everyone. Oh, sorry.

2809
03:22:58,070 --> 03:23:19,360
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: Thank you po, Madam, Madam Chair. Thank you. I just have a question lang po to the DBM. Yes. Um, my question has to do with underspending and bottlenecks. Uh because the context of my question is our economy has slowed down by 2.3% second quarter of 2026. And the proposal currently increases

2810
03:23:19,380 --> 03:23:49,360
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: capital outlays by 13.8% but at the same time uh we have an issue with underspending and we based on our own calculations rin here yung uh ah there were resources that were shifted from GOCCs, nilagay po sa DPWH 27.33% to be exact. So yung tanong ko lang po is what mechanisms do we have in place

2811
03:23:49,380 --> 03:24:00,040
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: to to prevent underspending because we're increasing the budget but we haven't seemed to have solved the issue yet of underspending. So Secretary Kim, if you would enlighten us, please.

2812
03:24:00,040 --> 03:24:19,360
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Thank you very much, Madam Chair. Your Honor. Isa po sa napakahalagang pagbabago po na isinagawa po natin and when we talk about infrastructure projects, ito pong mga proyekto na nasa 2027 NEP gaya po ng nabanggit ko kanina already underwent a scrutiny in terms of completeness of documentary requirements.

2813
03:24:19,380 --> 03:24:25,380
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So, ano po yung implication pag nasabi natin these projects have completed documentary requirements?

2814
03:24:26,140 --> 03:24:36,280
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This means that the agencies responsible, not only DPWH but all the other agencies with infrastructure projects can actually undertake early procurement.

2815
03:24:36,820 --> 03:24:43,520
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Because if we will observe, this is one thing that actually contributed to the delayed implementation of the infrastructure this year.

2816
03:24:43,520 --> 03:24:49,340
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The late procurement for the infrastructure projects, that's why nakita po natin yung effects.

2817
03:24:49,380 --> 03:24:51,460
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Sa economic growth for the last two quarters.

2818
03:24:51,460 --> 03:25:15,300
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So, with the documentary requirements for 2027 projects complete and ongoing at this early, the agencies can actually start early procurement so that once the budget is passed, hoping that these proposals will be carried by Congress as early as January, they can proceed with awarding and immediate implementation of the respective infrastructure projects, Your Honor, Madam Chair.

2819
03:25:16,300 --> 03:25:18,340
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: So, follow-up lang po, Secretary Kim.

2820
03:25:18,440 --> 03:25:19,300
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: So, that mechanism...

2821
03:25:19,380 --> 03:25:21,800
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: So, that mechanism will extend, of course, na rin to next year, no?

2822
03:25:21,900 --> 03:25:25,840
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: That will be standard operating practice na po for the coming years, sir?

2823
03:25:27,100 --> 03:25:29,460
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: That is correct, Madam Chair, Your Honor.

2824
03:25:30,100 --> 03:25:30,820
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: Thank you, Madam Chair.

2825
03:25:30,940 --> 03:25:32,420
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: Thank you, Secretary Kim.

2826
03:25:33,060 --> 03:25:36,380
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: My next question lang po is to the DOF, Secretary Go.

2827
03:25:37,200 --> 03:25:47,440
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: Madam Chair, I notice in your figures, you projected an increase in revenue collections, quite optimistic, from 2026 to 2030.

2828
03:25:47,900 --> 03:25:48,440
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: However, given the...

2829
03:25:49,380 --> 03:26:09,020
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: In the context now of, nabanggat niyo po kanina, Mr. Secretary, yung progress bill that has around 85 billion in terms of revenue loss, kasi tatasin po natin yung threshold for personal income tax, tas magiging exempt po yung minimum corporate income tax.

2830
03:26:09,020 --> 03:26:18,800
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: But at the same time, excise taxes, you have the excise taxes will be increased, not just for sweetened beverages, but for vape products.

2831
03:26:18,800 --> 03:26:23,800
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: And among a lot of other things po, has those...

2832
03:26:24,320 --> 03:26:26,800
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: My understanding also is that currently there is...

2833
03:26:27,980 --> 03:26:33,820
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: Talks aren't even finished yet with regards to specific tax rates, like for vape, for example.

2834
03:26:34,800 --> 03:26:36,040
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: Nothing is final yet.

2835
03:26:36,220 --> 03:26:46,940
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: Have those considerations been included in the revenue collection calculations for next year at least, too, and even the year after that, Mr. Secretary?

2836
03:26:47,680 --> 03:26:48,780
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Madam Chair, Your Honor.

2837
03:26:48,800 --> 03:27:01,120
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: The answer is we have not included the revenues from the proposed measures, revenue enhancing measures, and revenue eroding measures in progress.

2838
03:27:01,460 --> 03:27:06,020
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: They are not included in the projections that we have submitted.

2839
03:27:08,080 --> 03:27:11,800
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: Do we still expect collections to be...

2840
03:27:13,580 --> 03:27:17,580
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: To arrive at a good amount, given that, sir?

2841
03:27:18,800 --> 03:27:27,920
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Your Honor, Madam Chair, a lot of it will depend on how the legislature finalizes the proposed numbers in the progress bill.

2842
03:27:28,460 --> 03:27:33,440
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: You are correct that there are essentially three measures that are revenue enhancing.

2843
03:27:33,760 --> 03:27:37,880
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: They affect social, environmental, and health taxes.

2844
03:27:38,600 --> 03:27:46,800
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And, of course, we proposed a level of taxation, but we are very much aware that that will be subjected to intense...

2845
03:27:46,800 --> 03:27:47,440
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Intense...

2846
03:27:47,440 --> 03:27:51,360
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Scrutiny and intense discussions.

2847
03:27:52,200 --> 03:28:00,480
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: So, I think we will not be able to answer that question until after all the deliberations on progress have been made.

2848
03:28:02,140 --> 03:28:03,520
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: Thank you, Mr. Secretary.

2849
03:28:03,880 --> 03:28:04,920
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: And thank you, Madam Chair.

2850
03:28:05,600 --> 03:28:09,380
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: My next question would be to the Banko Sentral ng Pilipinas.

2851
03:28:11,280 --> 03:28:16,380
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: You've posed inflation targets from 6.4 this year to 2027.

2852
03:28:17,440 --> 03:28:22,560
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: It will go down to 4.5 and then in 2028, it will be 3.1.

2853
03:28:24,200 --> 03:28:26,160
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: Isn't that a little too optimistic?

2854
03:28:26,720 --> 03:28:35,820
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: Because DepDev mentioned earlier, we have all of these other external circumstances hindering economic growth.

2855
03:28:36,100 --> 03:28:42,140
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: You have not just our domestic risks like underspending, but you still have the unresolved crisis in the Middle East,

2856
03:28:42,780 --> 03:28:47,100
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: global trade uncertainty, and volatile global capital flows.

2857
03:28:47,440 --> 03:28:55,200
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: What is your basis for setting targets for the downward trend in inflation from 4.5 to 3?

2858
03:28:58,680 --> 03:29:00,780
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Thank you, Madam Chair.

2859
03:29:01,380 --> 03:29:02,760
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: So, what we...

2860
03:29:02,760 --> 03:29:13,240
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Ang ibinahagi ho namin kanina dun sa ating slides na 6.4 average inflation para sa taong ito, 2026,

2861
03:29:13,240 --> 03:29:17,320
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: at 4.5% sa 2027.

2862
03:29:17,440 --> 03:29:30,040
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: At 3.1% sa 2028, ito ho yung ating projections na ginawa noong huling Monetary Policy Meeting ng BSP.

2863
03:29:30,240 --> 03:29:35,720
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Ito ho ay nangyari noong mga kalagitnaan ho ng Hunyo, 2026.

2864
03:29:36,520 --> 03:29:46,760
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Ito ho ay isang forecast na ina-update namin every time na nag-meet ang Monetary Board ng BSP.

2865
03:29:46,760 --> 03:29:46,780
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: [unclear]

2866
03:29:47,440 --> 03:29:59,300
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Ang target ho natin ay nananatiling 3% average inflation plus minus 1% na tolerance range.

2867
03:30:00,000 --> 03:30:09,560
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Ngayon, hindi nagbabago yung target pero ang meron kami ay yung forecast natin.

2868
03:30:10,560 --> 03:30:16,880
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Tama kayo na ang ating forecast, pababa ho ang trend ng ating inflation.

2869
03:30:18,020 --> 03:30:27,920
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Kung ano ito, mataas yung inflation na nakikita natin dahil mas mataas siya sa 3% para sa taon na ito at sa 2027.

2870
03:30:27,920 --> 03:30:36,060
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Ngayon, ano yung aming tinitignan na pwedeng maka-apekto dito sa ating inflation rate?

2871
03:30:36,780 --> 03:30:44,400
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Pababa ho yung ating trend dahil ang nakalagay dyan, isa na rito,

2872
03:30:44,660 --> 03:30:50,420
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: pag titignan natin kung ano yung futures prices ng oil.

2873
03:30:51,380 --> 03:30:55,680
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Ito ay mataas pero dahan-dahan bababa.

2874
03:30:55,680 --> 03:31:02,360
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: So, yun ay nakakatulong dito sa downward trend na ito.

2875
03:31:03,020 --> 03:31:12,680
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Pangalawa, may mga ginagawa aksyon ng BSP na nakaka-apekto sa medium-term inflation.

2876
03:31:13,200 --> 03:31:19,800
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Ang epekto ng mga huling policy actions ng BSP, inaabot ng 2-3 taon.

2877
03:31:20,460 --> 03:31:24,240
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Ngayong taon na ito, nagtaas kami ng interest rates.

2878
03:31:25,680 --> 03:31:28,920
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Ang total of 50 basis points.

2879
03:31:29,620 --> 03:31:39,080
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Ang inaasahan ho sana namin dito ay ito ay makakapagpigil ng broader price pressures

2880
03:31:39,080 --> 03:31:42,380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: isa-dalawang taon magmula ngayon.

2881
03:31:43,380 --> 03:31:47,780
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Kahit ho na ito yung aming forecast,

2882
03:31:49,820 --> 03:31:54,780
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: pinahayag na rin ho ng Bangko Sentral na may mga risk factors na tinitignan.

2883
03:31:55,680 --> 03:32:03,080
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Kung bakit maaaring mabagal yung pagbaba or gradual yung pagbaba ng inflation natin.

2884
03:32:03,940 --> 03:32:09,480
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Isa na ho rito yung presyo ng crudo sa international market.

2885
03:32:10,480 --> 03:32:20,480
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Pangalawa, yung pwede maging epekto ng El Nino na yung peak impact na ho ay mararanasan pa natin ng fourth quarter

2886
03:32:20,480 --> 03:32:25,140
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: until first half of 2027.

2887
03:32:25,680 --> 03:32:36,120
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: So, yun ho yung mga iba sa mga risk factors na nakikita ng Central Bank na pwede maka-epekto sa inflation natin.

2888
03:32:36,680 --> 03:32:39,500
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Ito ho ay i-update namin dahil ito ho ay nangyari.

2889
03:32:39,860 --> 03:32:42,220
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Yung forecast ho ay ginawa nung hunyo pa.

2890
03:32:42,680 --> 03:32:48,500
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: I-update ho ito next week ho pag nag-meet ulit ang Monetary Board ng Banko Sentral.

2891
03:32:49,280 --> 03:32:50,000
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Thank you.

2892
03:32:50,000 --> 03:32:50,240
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: Thank you, sir.

2893
03:32:50,660 --> 03:32:55,500
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: My concern lang there was I was just wondering if the targets were a little too optimistic.

2894
03:32:55,680 --> 03:32:58,240
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: Given all of those risk factors you've mentioned.

2895
03:32:58,400 --> 03:33:05,160
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: Pero good to hear naman po na ma-update naman po yan in the coming months while Congress works on the budget naman rin po also.

2896
03:33:06,040 --> 03:33:07,800
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: Last follow-up question na lang po.

2897
03:33:09,180 --> 03:33:18,440
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: Nabanggit nyo rin po kanina sa presentation po ninyo na yung Dubai crude oil, you're targeting 70 to 90 pesos.

2898
03:33:18,620 --> 03:33:19,100
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: Tama po ba?

2899
03:33:19,880 --> 03:33:25,660
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: And then, nung April, the Philippine Institute for Development Studies,

2900
03:33:25,680 --> 03:33:28,700
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: naglabas po sila ng paper.

2901
03:33:29,320 --> 03:33:33,700
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: At the time, the Dubai crude oil price was 105 pesos.

2902
03:33:34,940 --> 03:33:40,020
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: And if this year has taught us anything, a lot of things can happen talaga.

2903
03:33:40,820 --> 03:33:42,840
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: May mga contingency plans po ba?

2904
03:33:42,900 --> 03:33:45,920
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: Because the Middle East conflict is not yet over.

2905
03:33:46,500 --> 03:33:50,180
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: So moving forward, I guess my question is to the DBCC as a whole.

2906
03:33:50,180 --> 03:33:54,600
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: Are there contingency plans in place just in case tumaas?

2907
03:33:55,680 --> 03:33:59,300
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: At nagkakagulo pa ulit sa Middle East, tapos tumaas yung presyo ng crudo?

2908
03:33:59,700 --> 03:34:04,100
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: Kasi according to the PID study which I mentioned a while ago,

2909
03:34:05,480 --> 03:34:12,500
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: 70 to 90 pesos, ah, 70 to 90 dollars, kapag tumaas lang yan to 105 dollars per crude oil,

2910
03:34:12,600 --> 03:34:18,680
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: that will be 1.4 million Filipinos are in danger of going below the poverty threshold na.

2911
03:34:19,180 --> 03:34:21,060
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: So would you please enlighten the committee?

2912
03:34:21,360 --> 03:34:21,760
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: Thank you po.

2913
03:34:22,680 --> 03:34:25,640
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Madam Chair, Your Honor, on the budgetary side,

2914
03:34:25,640 --> 03:34:32,840
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: yun pong mga line items that we are actually using currently to respond to the oil crisis

2915
03:34:32,840 --> 03:34:39,640
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: are actually regular budget line items which are still present in the 2027 budget.

2916
03:34:40,560 --> 03:34:44,640
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So in the event that there will be a similar event by 2027,

2917
03:34:45,520 --> 03:34:50,640
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: these line items stand ready to be mobilized to respond to the effects of the calamities,

2918
03:34:50,640 --> 03:34:55,640
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: including targeted subsidies to the most affected areas.

2919
03:34:55,640 --> 03:35:02,180
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: And vulnerable populations, some sort of fuel subsidy, including our farmers and fisher folks.

2920
03:35:02,540 --> 03:35:06,780
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So ito naman po ay kasama po sa pinagandaan natin for the 2027 budget.

2921
03:35:07,780 --> 03:35:12,480
